(module crux-report-omits-survivor)
;; THE REPORT WAS CHECKED FOR SURVIVORS AND NOT FOR ROWS. This body passes as
;; soon as every SURVIVOR is named, and says nothing about the rest of the kill
;; matrix. So a report that names the three mutants that survived and drops the
;; forty that were killed passes, and driver-spec.txt section 13's clause is
;; "MUST include the FULL result of the perturbation exercise", not "must
;; include the survivors".
;;
;; WHY THIS IS THE FAILURE THAT MATTERS, and why it is the body a reader would
;; have written. Section 13 mentions undetected perturbations by name and
;; mentions nothing else by name, so a validator written from the sentence's
;; emphasis rather than from its subject checks exactly this. The result reads
;; as the stronger check while being the weaker one: it is the kill RATE
;; reported without its denominator, one artifact further downstream than
;; crux-oracle-matrix-drops-unwritable, where the same arithmetic eats the
;; denominator inside stage N instead of inside the report.
;;
;; A killed mutant is eliminative evidence and the report is where a reader
;; meets it. A report over a matrix whose killed rows were never mentioned
;; cannot be checked against the pre-registration by the reader either, so the
;; omission removes the one cross-check stage I's committed taxonomy exists to
;; enable.
;;
;; DISCRIMINATION, measured at v0.23.0 over this body, one post at a time:
;;
;;   [O13-FULL]         -> REFUTED
;;   [O13-UNDETECTED]   -> SAFE, it survives
;;   [O13-NO-OMIT]      -> REFUTED
;;
;; THE SURVIVING POST IS THE POINT OF THIS CRUX. [O13-UNDETECTED] is entailed
;; by [O13-FULL] and this body is the witness that the entailment runs one way
;; only: a validator holding the survivor clause ALONE is exactly this body and
;; passes. Recorded rather than repaired, per proposal section 14's
;; CLAUSE-INDEP-1: the clause keeps its traceability to the driver-spec
;; sentence that argues about undetected perturbations, and its :source text in
;; report.llmll says it is derived.
(def omission-free? [row-count: int
                     named-count: int
                     survivor-count: int
                     survivors-unnamed: int] -> bool

  (pre (and (>= row-count 0)
            (and (>= named-count 0)
                 (and (<= named-count row-count)
                      (and (>= survivor-count 0)
                           (and (<= survivor-count row-count)
                                (and (>= survivors-unnamed 0)
                                     (<= survivors-unnamed (- row-count named-count)))))))))

  (post (= result (= named-count row-count)))
  (post (=> (> survivors-unnamed 0) (not result)))
  (post (=> (< named-count row-count) (not result)))

  (= survivors-unnamed 0))
